    "committer": "tgirke <tgirke@citrus.ucr.edu>",
    "message": "Regenerate the 8-gene paralog fixture: complete at last\n\nThe fixture has shipped covering 6 of its 8 genes since 2026-08-08,\nkeeping test-idTranslation.R:123 red. Twelve regeneration attempts across\ntwo days were refused by the completeness guard, and the pattern in them\nwas the diagnosis: the missing set varied from attempt to attempt except\nfor FGFR1, which failed every single time - and failed by timeout rather\nthan by HTTP 500. FGFR1 has by far the most paralogs of the eight, so the\nlargest response, and it needs longer than .dtiApiGET's 120s.\n\nRegenerated with the per-request timeout raised to 300s for the\ngeneration run only: 128 rows covering all 8 genes (FGFR1 53, FGF21 21,\nNLRP3 20, ADIPOR1/2 10 each, IL1B 7, KLB 4, TFEB 3). Same data, just\nfetched with more patience; the shipped completeness guard still decided\nwhether anything was written, and it accepted this one on the first\nattempt.\n\nVerified off the fixture rather than off a lucky live call: with\n.dtiApiGET forced to signal failure for every request, the batch call\nrecovers all 8 genes from the fixture with dtiCached TRUE.\ntest-idTranslation.R now 20 pass, 0 fail - the first clean run of that\nfile since 2026-08-08.\n\nWorth following up separately: a user calling getEnsemblParalogs(\"FGFR1\")\ndirectly gets the same 120s timeout with no fallback behind it, so the\ndefault deserves a second look.\n",
    "time": 1786938258
  },
